{"_data": [{"contents": [{"content": "", "type": "lesson_name"}, {"content": "Documentation of Program Code", "type": "unit_name"}, {"content": 5, "type": "position"}, {"content": "stub", "type": "origin"}, {"content": 2, "type": "lesson"}, {"content": "A1.2", "type": "level"}], "type": "metadata"}, {"contents": [{"content": "false", "type": "test"}], "type": "achievment_test"}, {"contents": [{"content": "These are words you hear or use to talk about documentation of Program Code.", "type": "text"}], "type": "target_word_describer"}, {"contents": [{"content": "Understand key information about the concepts, principles, and methodologies in simple spoken and written situations.  Talk about programming techniques, use cases, kinds, and sequences in simple spoken and written situations.", "type": "primary"}, {"content": "Communicates effectively in English about the communicative topics for this level through the use of appropriate basic vocabulary and grammatical structures.  Identifies general aspects related to Software Programming in short written or spoken conversations about past experiences.", "type": "secondary_1"}], "type": "objectives"}, {"content": "enpe7n2le02ob05re1img01.jpg", "type": "background_image"}, {"contents": [{"content": "program listing", "type": "name"}, {"content": "the list of programs, code and different files a computer may have", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: It explains that documentation code refers to the program listings or technical manuals describing the operation and use of programs.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "enpe7n2le02ob05aud01", "type": "audio"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"content": "guess", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to give an answer or opinion about something  even when you are not sure about the correct answer ", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(verb)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: I guess it does not help inexperienced people like me.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "enpe7n2le02ob05aud02", "type": "audio"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"content": "main", "type": "name"}, {"content": "principal or more important", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(adjective)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: it has two main categories.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "enpe7n2le02ob05aud03", "type": "audio"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"content": "maintenance", "type": "name"}, {"content": "specific work  that a computer hardware or software requires to keep running in well performance conditions", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: It also focuses on documentation for programmers involved in software development and maintenance.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "enpe7n2le02ob05aud04", "type": "audio"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"content": "facilities", "type": "name"}, {"content": "Equipment or services arranged in a partcular place for people to  perform specific tasks", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: With punched cards, programmers had minimal facilities for incorporating comments.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "enpe7n2le02ob05aud05", "type": "audio"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"content": "switch", "type": "name"}, {"content": "To change, exchange or replace one person or thing with another", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(verb)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: Documenting code and adding comments became easier when programmers switched from punch card input to the use of keyboards.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "enpe7n2le02ob05aud06", "type": "audio"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"content": "Find more information about the benefits of implementing documentation of program code.  ", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Choose the most important ideas. ", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Organize the information in a poster. ", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Explain to your partners about the benefits of implementing documentation of program code. ", "type": "text"}], "type": "takeaway_extension"}, {"contents": [{"content": "I find information about the documentation of program code. ", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I choose the most important ideas. ", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I organize the information in a poster. ", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I explain to my partners the benefits of implementing documentation of program code. ", "type": "text"}], "type": "takeaway_assessment"}, {"contents": [{"content": "Indefinite Pronouns", "type": "heading"}, {"content": "We use -body, -one, -thing, -where to refer to people, places and things in a general way. We write them as one single word.", "type": "describer"}, {"content": "<span class= \"strong\">  Indefinite pronouns </span>  don't refer to a specific person, place, or thing. <span class= \"strong\">  Indefinite pronouns </span>  are formed with a quantifier or distributive.</br></br>  For example: <i>any, some, every and no.</i></br></br>  The differences in their meanings are the same as the differences between some, any, every\u00a0and\u00a0no.</br></br>  SOME: is used in affirmative sentences, <span class= \"strong\">  Indefinite pronouns </span>  using some are used to describe an indefinite quantity.</br></br>  EVERY: is used to describe a complete quantity. </br></br>  NO: the pronouns with no are used to describe an absence. </br></br> <span class= \"strong\">  Indefinite pronouns </span>  with no are regularly used in affirmative sentences with a negative sense.</br></br>", "type": "text"}, {"content": "{\"rows\":5,\"columns\":4,\"cells\":[\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" \\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<div align=\\\"center\\\"><strong>Person</strong></div>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<div align=\\\"center\\\"><strong>Place</strong></div>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<div align=\\\"center\\\"><strong>Thing</strong></div>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<div align=\\\"center\\\"><strong>All</strong></div>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"everyone</br>everybody\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"everywhere\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"everything\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<div align=\\\"center\\\"><strong>Part (positive)</strong></div>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"someone</br>somebody\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"somewhere\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"somewhere\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<div align=\\\"center\\\"><strong>Part (negative)</strong></div>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"anyone</br>anybody\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"anywhere\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"anywhere\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<div align=\\\"center\\\"><strong>None</strong></div>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"no one</br>nobody\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"nowhere\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"nothing\\\"}\"],\"styles\":\" intro_table_border instruction_table_background\"}", "type": "table"}, {"content": "I do not know anything about it. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "Is there anything that a person who is not a software developer can understand? ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "It sounds something similar to what programmers do with JAVA and C+ ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "Tell me something else.", "type": "example"}], "type": "learning_points"}, {"contents": [{"content": "Auxiliary + Not  Contractions", "type": "heading"}, {"content": "When you use the simple present and you want to express a negative connotation of your sentence you can use the <strong>auxiliary</strong> of the grammar tense and add \u201cnot\u201d.</br> Remember that in English, we use <strong>contractions</strong> when a conversation or a writing is not formal.", "type": "describer"}, {"content": "For each grammar tense, there is a corresponding auxiliary verb. </br></br>  Let's have a look of the possibilities, remember that when making negative sentences with the verb to be, you need to use contractions.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "{\"rows\":3,\"columns\":2,\"cells\":[\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<div align=\\\"center\\\">I:</div>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<i><div align=\\\"center\\\"><strong>I'm not</strong></div></i>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<div align=\\\"center\\\">He, she , it:</div>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<i><div align=\\\"center\\\"><strong>Isn't </strong></div></i>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<div align=\\\"center\\\">We, they, you:</div>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<i><div align=\\\"center\\\"><strong>Aren't</strong></div></i>\\\"}\"],\"styles\":\"\"}", "type": "table"}, {"content": "For the simple present with other verbs, you need to choose one auxiliary according to the person doing the action or the subject.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "{\"rows\":2,\"columns\":2,\"cells\":[\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<div align=\\\"center\\\">I, We, You They:</div>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<i><div align=\\\"center\\\"><strong>Don't</strong></div></i>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<div align=\\\"center\\\">He, She, It:</div>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<i><div align=\\